[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m not in the translation: the smoke test `both_binaries_run` asserted the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reference output for input `1 2` was `-1\n`, when `1 | ~2 == 1 | -3 == -3`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Fixed by correcting the expected literal to `-3\n`. The differential
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m assertions for that same input passed throughout — the Rust and C outputs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m agreed with each other before and after the fix.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
